---
import { STATS, STAT_KEYS } from "@bt/core";
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";

const labels = STAT_KEYS.map((key) => STATS[key].label);
---

<Page
  title="Football Higher or Lower — Bigger Than Game"
  description="A free football higher or lower game with retired legends. Guess whether the hidden stat is higher or lower — and watch out, because the stat keeps changing."
>
  <h1>
    Football <em>higher or lower</em>
  </h1>
  <p>
    Bigger Than is a free football higher or lower game. Two football legends appear side by side
    with a stat between them. You can see one player's number; guess whether the other's is higher
    or lower. There's nothing to sign up for or download, and it plays in the browser on a phone or
    a computer.
  </p>
  <a class="cta" href="/">
    Play now
  </a>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    Each round shows two retired players. A wheel lands on a stat, the first player's figure is
    revealed, and you pick <strong>Higher</strong> or <strong>Lower</strong> for the second. Get it
    right and the player you just guessed stays on to face someone new. Get it wrong and the run is
    over. Your score is how many you got right in a row.
  </p>

  <h2>The stat keeps changing</h2>
  <p>
    Most higher or lower games ask the same question all the way through. Bigger Than switches stat
    every few rounds. You beat someone on international caps, and the next question is about
    Instagram followers, where a veteran defender loses to a winger with a boot deal. Knowing which
    players were great is only half of it; you also need to know what they were great at.
  </p>
  <p>The stats are:</p>
  <ul>
    {labels.map((label) => (
      <li>{label}</li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p>
    Each one is defined on the <a href="/about">about page</a>, including exactly what counts as a
    club trophy.
  </p>

  <h2>Legends only</h2>
  <p>
    Every player is retired. Their caps, goals, trophies and transfer fees are settled, so the
    answers don't change from one week to the next. The game is for people who follow football
    rather than casual quizzers, so expect defenders, goalkeepers and midfielders from past decades,
    not only the famous strikers.
  </p>

  <h2>No timer</h2>
  <p>
    Friendly Mode has no clock. Take as long as you like over each answer. It uses every player and
    every stat, and nothing is ranked.
  </p>

  <h2>Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Read the plaque before you pick. When the wheel spins, the question has changed.</li>
    <li>
      Club goals and international goals are counted separately. A great club scorer can have a thin
      international record.
    </li>
    <li>
      Transfer fees are shown with the year and aren't adjusted for inflation, so a record fee from
      decades ago can still lose to an ordinary modern one.
    </li>
    <li>
      Instagram followers reward global fame, not career achievement. Some of the greatest players
      have the smallest followings.
    </li>
    <li>Goalkeepers are never asked about goals, but they are asked about appearances.</li>
  </ul>

  <a class="cta" href="/">
    Start a run
  </a>
</Page>
